  applicantName: Alex Morgan
  body: '<b>ALEX MORGAN</b>

    Applying for: Junior Gameplay Programmer


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    {title_pixelforge}
    - PixelForge Studios

    {dates_pixelforge}


    Junior Developer - Brightline
    Games

    {dates_brightline}


    <b>SKILLS</b>

    {skill_csharp}, {skill_unity},
    debugging


    <b>CERTIFICATIONS</b>

    {cert_unity}


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {reference}'
  claims:
  - id: title_pixelforge
    text: Lead Software Architect
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 2
    designerNote: Exaggerated title for someone with ~3 years of junior experience.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your title was Lead Software Architect. What did that involve?
      answer: Oh, the usual architect stuff. I {t_junior}, mostly fixing bugs. And
        I {t_meetings}.
      demeanor: 2
      phrases:
      - id: t_junior
        text: was the most junior person on the team
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: ...Okay. The title was more of a vibe. My manager said I
          could call myself whatever I wanted on LinkedIn.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
      - id: t_meetings
        text: went to a lot of meetings
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: So many meetings. Architects love meetings. That part is
          100% true.
        callOutDemeanor: 2
    goodQuestion:
      question: Lead Software Architect is impressive. Tell me more about it.
      answer: Thanks! I, uh, mostly did programming and debugging, honestly.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases: []
  - id: dates_pixelforge
    text: Mar 2021 - Aug 2024
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 1
    designerNote: Overlaps with the Brightline Games job (2021-2022).
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your PixelForge dates overlap with Brightline Games. Were you working
        two jobs?
      answer: That's a typo! I started at PixelForge right after I left Brightline
        {d_2020}.
      demeanor: 3
      phrases:
      - id: d_2020
        text: in 2020
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: 2022! I meant 2022. Numbers are hard. I'm a programmer,
          not a... number person.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
    goodQuestion:
      question: So you were at PixelForge until 2024?
      answer: Yes, until the company moved to another state.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: dates_brightline
    text: Jan 2019 - Jun 2022
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 1
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Why did you leave Brightline Games?
      answer: I wanted to move into {b_gameplay}, and Brightline only made tools.
      demeanor: 0
      phrases:
      - id: b_gameplay
        text: gameplay programming
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Yes? Gameplay programming. That's... the job I'm applying
          for.
        callOutDemeanor: 0
    goodQuestion:
      question: How was your time at Brightline Games?
      answer: Great team. I learned most of what I know there.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_csharp
    text: C#
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: How much C# have you actually written?
      answer: Plenty. Gameplay scripts, editor tools, a whole save system. Ask me
        anything.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
    goodQuestion:
      question: What's your favourite thing you've built in C#?
      answer: A save system for a small RPG. It was a fun puzzle to get right.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_unity
    text: Unity
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Have you really shipped anything in Unity?
      answer: A couple of small game jam games. Nothing commercial, but they're finished.
      demeanor: 0
      phrases: []
    goodQuestion:
      question: Tell me about your Unity projects.
      answer: Mostly small jam projects. I handled the programming and debugging.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: cert_unity
    text: Unity Certified Expert - Programmer
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 3
    designerNote: No certification ID listed; expert-level cert is unlikely for a
      junior.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Can you give me the ID for your Unity Expert certification?
      answer: I... don't have it on me. I'm pretty sure I passed. Mostly sure.
      demeanor: 3
      phrases: []
    goodQuestion:
      question: An Expert certification, nice. When did you take it?
      answer: A while ago. I don't really remember exactly when.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases: []
  - id: reference
    text: Jordan Morgan, former manager
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 5
    designerNote: 'Same surname as the applicant: actually their mom.'
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Jordan Morgan has the same last name as you. Are you related?
      answer: That's a coincidence! Morgan is a {r_common} name. Why would you even
        ask that?
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: r_common
        text: really common
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: It IS common! There are like... several of us!
        callOutDemeanor: 4
    goodQuestion:
      question: Can Jordan Morgan vouch for your work?
      answer: Absolutely. Jordan has known me {r_life} career.
      demeanor: 2
      phrases:
      - id: r_life
        text: my whole li- my whole
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: ...my whole LIFE. Fine. Jordan is my mom. She was a very
          good manager, though.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
  referenceLetter: 'To whom it may concern,


